## 3. ALMA Observations: 

Follow-up ALMA Band 6 observations were carried out on the five multiple images in RXCJ0600-2007 from January to August 2022 as a part of Cycle 8 program (#2021.1.00055.S, PI: S. Fujimoto), targeting their \[C ii\] 158-$\mu$m emission line. Because the \[C ii\] line was detected from the brightest multiple images of $z6\_1,2$ (arc) and the *Cosmic Grapes* in the previous ALCS data cube with relatively short exposure, these follow-up observations aimed to perform deep, high-resolution \[C ii\] line spectroscopy to probe the internal structures and kinematics. The configurations of C43-2 and C43-5 were used, with the on-source integration times of 49.4 mins and 107.8 mins, respectively, for $z6\_1,2$ (arc) and $z6\_2$. Note that the \[C ii\] line was not clearly detected in the other two multiple images of $z6\_4$ and $z6\_5$ in the previous ALCS data cube, and thus, additional follow-up observations for $z6\_4$ and $z6\_5$ were also designed to detect the \[C ii\] line to obtain the spectroscopic confirmations of these multiple images. The C43-2 configuration was used, with the on-source integration time of 12.6 mins for each.

